Description:
    Generates the Geo SSF (self-service framework) replication and verification boilerplate for
    a new replicator: replicator, registry and state models, registry finder, GraphQL
    resolver/type, ops feature flags, tracking-DB and main-DB migrations, database dictionaries,
    factories, specs, and the framework-list patches.

    Two concrete generators share this base:
      - geo:blob_replicator        for CarrierWave-backed blobs (optionally --upload-partition)
      - geo:repository_replicator  for Git repository types (wires the existing model in place)

    Pass the snake_case replicable name as NAME. --model-class is required (in blob
    --upload-partition mode it defaults to the CamelCase of NAME).

Example:
    Git repository replicator:
    rails generate geo:repository_replicator group_wiki_repository \
      --table-name=group_wiki_repositories \
      --sharding-key=namespace_id \
      --milestone=19.1 --model-class=GroupWikiRepository

    Blob replicator (upload partition):
    rails generate geo:blob_replicator vulnerability_remediation_upload \
      --table-name=vulnerability_remediation_uploads \
      --sharding-key=project_id \
      --milestone=19.1 \
      --upload-partition

    Non-partition replicable (model-class required):
    rails generate geo:blob_replicator ci_secure_file \
      --table-name=ci_secure_files --sharding-key=project_id \
      --milestone=18.10 --model-class=Ci::SecureFile

    Multiple sharding keys:
    rails generate geo:blob_replicator ai_vectorizable_file_upload \
      --table-name=ai_vectorizable_file_uploads \
      --sharding-key=namespace_id project_id \
      --milestone=18.11 --upload-partition

    After a rebase, re-apply the framework patches and regenerate the derived docs without
    recreating files or migrations. Reset any conflicting generated or patched artifacts
    (introspection_result.json, the OpenAPI specs, gitlab.pot, db dictionaries, GraphQL reference,
    the geo_node/site status fixtures, and the API and prometheus docs) to the master version
    first, then run:
    rails generate geo:blob_replicator vulnerability_remediation_upload \
      --table-name=vulnerability_remediation_uploads \
      --sharding-key=project_id \
      --milestone=19.1 --upload-partition --only-post-generate
